        "original_id": "67903bc1-552e-5311-81b9-92e07cd4b38e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bill Walton, John Wooden, Brad Nessler, Tom Tolbert, Lucious Harris\n- Organizations: UCLA Bruins, UCLA, Nets, ABC\n- Events: NCAA national championships, 2002 NBA Finals, 2003 NBA Finals\n- Topics: College Player of the Year Awards, Division I national titles, sports broadcasting\n\nFacts:\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton became known for playing for John Wooden's UCLA Bruins.\n- In the early 1970s, Bill Walton won three successive College Player of the Year Awards and led the UCLA Bruins to two Division I national titles.\n- John Wooden, nicknamed the \"Wizard of Westwood,\" won ten NCAA national championships in 12 years as head coach at UCLA, including a record seven in a row.\n- Lucious Harris played in the 2002 NBA Finals and the 2003 NBA Finals as a member of the Nets.\n- The 2003 NBA Finals were broadcast on ABC in the United States, with Brad Nessler, Bill Walton, and Tom Tolbert as announcers.",
